    s__LICHEN_CARD(py_str("White, thin, shiny skin around the vulva that tears or splits is lichen sclerosus: a skin condition, not an infection and not an STI, and it does not clear up on its own. See a GP or a sexual health clinic rather than waiting, because a strong steroid ointment settles it and untreated it can scar and tighten the skin - and it is very often put down to thrush for years before anyone looks at the skin. Meanwhile wash with water only, no soap, wipes or douching, pat dry, and use plain petroleum jelly as a barrier. Do not use a thrush cream on it unless a doctor says so, and go back if it hurts to sit or to have sex, or if you notice a lump or a bleeding patch."));
